# The pointer on a double-size line selects the doubled character drawn
# under it: display column C of a line of double size is the line's own
# column C / 2. A selection on either line of a double-height pair
# selects the pair's characters on both lines, and the copy takes the
# pair's text once, from its top line. Row 0 is a top line (ESC # 3),
# row 1 its bottom line (ESC # 4), row 2 a double-width line (ESC # 6)
# and row 3 a line of the normal size, on a screen 10 columns wide.
# spec: ADR-1308 D1, "Selection on a double-size line follows the cursor's rule": "On a double-height pair, a selection that covers a character on either line of the pair highlights both halves of that doubled character. Copying a selection that covers both lines of a pair gives the pair's text once, from its top line. On a double-width line, the highlight covers both display cells of each character. The pointer maps a click or a drag on a double-size line to that line's own columns, which are half the screen's."
# covers: text.line-size, clipboard.selection
size 10 4
send "\e#3abcd\r\n\e#4abcd\r\n\e#6wxyz\r\n1234"
select start at 2,0
select to at 5,1
copy
select start at 0,0
select to at 9,3
copy
select start at 3,2
select to at 4,2
copy
select word at 7,1
copy
select line at 0,1
copy
select start at 2,1
select to at 3,1
copy
dump
